<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Shaykan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1883">1883</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of El Obeid · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdist-war">Mahdist War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Shaykan was fought on 3–5 November 1883 in the forest of Shaykan near El Obeid in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kordofan">Kordofan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a>'s Ansar surrounded and destroyed an Egyptian army under the British officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-hicks">William Hicks</a>, leaving few survivors. The victory gave the Mahdists control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-sudan">western Sudan</a> and large stocks of modern weapons, and convinced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to abandon the Sudan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-shaykan.jpg" alt="Battle of Shaykan" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_army_of_Hicks_Pasha_on_the_march.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
